{number: 41}
{title: Nothing but the Blood}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] What can wash away my sin?
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
What can make me whole again?
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [G] precious is the flow
That [D7] makes me white as snow;
No [G] other fount I know;
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] For my pardon this I see:
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
For my cleansing this my plea:
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Nothing can for sin atone:
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
Naught of good that I have done:
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[G] This is all my hope and peace:
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
This is all my righteousness:
[D7] Nothing but the blood of [G] Jesus.
{end_of_verse}
